ull,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.553131,"donor_log2fc":0.235935,"donor_lfcse":0.107949,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":0.0264084,"degas_log2fc":null,"degas_padj":null}],"modules":[{"cell_type":"Ast","gene_id":"ENSG00000176386","module":"turquoise","kme":0.0944214,"hub":false,"module_direction":"lower in AD","module_padj":0.796936,"module_significant":false},{"cell_type":"Ex","gene_id":"ENSG00000176386","module":"turquoise","kme":0.155607,"hub":false,"module_direction":"lower in AD","module_padj":0.524491,"module_significant":false},{"cell_type":"OPC","gene_id":"ENSG00000176386","module":"turquoise","kme":0.063275,"hub":false,"module_direction":"higher in AD","module_padj":0.680759,"module_significant":false},{"cell_type":"Oli","gene_id":"ENSG00000176386","module":"turquoise","kme":0.0545551,"hub":false,"module_direction":"higher in AD","module_padj":0.842971,"module_significant":false}],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000176386","entrez_id":["246184"],"uniprot":["Q8NHZ8"],"ncbi_summary":"The protein encoded by this gene is highly similar to Saccharomyces cerevisiae Cdc26, a component of cell cycle anaphase-promoting complex (APC). APC is composed of a group of highly conserved proteins and functions as a cell cycle-regulated ubiquitin-protein ligase. APC thus is responsible for the cell cycle regulated proteolysis of various proteins. [provided by RefSeq, Jul 2008].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q8NHZ8","text":"Component of the anaphase promoting complex/cyclosome (APC/C), a cell cycle-regulated E3 ubiquitin ligase that controls progression through the cell cycle (PubMed:18485873, PubMed:27120157, PubMed:27509861). Together with the RING-H2 protein ANAPC11, forms the catalytic component of the E3 ubiquitin ligase complex (PubMed:18485873, PubMed:27120157, PubMed:27509861). APC/C acts by mediating ubiquitination and subsequent degradation of target proteins: it mainly mediates the formation of 'Lys-11'-linked polyubiquitin chains and, to a lower extent, the formation of 'Lys-48'- and 'Lys-63'-linked polyubiquitin chains (PubMed:18485873). APC/C catalyzes assembly of branched 'Lys-11'-/'Lys-48'-linked branched ubiquitin chains on target proteins (PubMed:29033132). APC/C is activated by CDC20 in the metaphase/anaphase transition of cell cycle, targeting the degradation of cyclin B and securin (PubMed:27120157, PubMed:27509861). APC/C is regulated by the mitotic checkpoint complex (MCC), which inhibits APC/C and delays chromosome segregation (PubMed:27509861). May recruit the E2 ubiquitin-conjugating enzymes to the complex (PubMed:18485873)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}